<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Potions</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>quaff &lt;potion&gt;
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>quaff red potion
</pre>
<p>A potion holds up to three spells. Quaff it, and it is gone, and its 
spells are cast on you at the potion's own power, whatever your own 
skill. The most sought-after potions heal you, like the spells cure light 
wounds and heal; others protect you, cure poison, restore mana, or worse. 
To learn what a potion holds before you drink it, identify it (see 
<a cmd='#'>Help Identify</a>).
</p><p>You must carry the potion. You can quaff while resting, and in the middle 
of a fight, but drinking there costs you two rounds of attacks.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Identify</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Scrolls</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Wands</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Spells</a>
</pre>




</div>